@prefix rk:   <https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .


<https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk/bfo-stub> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "BFO stub"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Bare declarations of the external terms the module references, for
reasoning in environments where the real imports cannot be resolved.

This file asserts no BFO axiom. It exists so the module's own axioms stay
checkable, and it is NOT a pass on conformance: an undeclared obo:BFO_0000050
is not an error in OWL, so every restriction built on it would go inert and a
run could report consistent for entirely the wrong reason. Any validation
report produced against this file must say so. Use tools/check_bfo.py to check
the alignment itself."""@en .

obo:BFO_0000050 a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "part of"@en .
obo:BFO_0000051 a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "has part"@en .
obo:BFO_0000015 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "process"@en .
obo:BFO_0000023 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "role"@en .
obo:BFO_0000017 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "realizable entity"@en .
obo:BFO_0000003 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "occurrent"@en .
obo:BFO_0000004 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "independent continuant"@en .
obo:IAO_0000030 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "information content entity"@en .
obo:IAO_0000033 a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "directive information entity"@en .
obo:IAO_0000115 a owl:AnnotationProperty ; rdfs:label "definition"@en .
obo:IAO_0000119 a owl:AnnotationProperty ; rdfs:label "definition source"@en .
obo:IAO_0000136 a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "is about"@en .
obo:RO_0000052 a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "characteristic of"@en .
